NAME
       statvfs, list_mounts - filesystem information

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/statvfs.h>

       int cervus_statvfs(const char *path, struct statvfs *st);
       int cervus_list_mounts(cervus_mount_t *out, int max);
       int statvfs(const char *path, struct statvfs *st);

DESCRIPTION
       Reports the block size, total, free and available blocks of the
       filesystem holding PATH. list_mounts enumerates every mount with
       its device, mount point and type.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENOENT   the path does not exist

SEE ALSO
       df(1), mount(2), stat(2)
